/*! \page code_mcstep User-Simulation Interface
  \brief Details the structural design of qmc::MCStep.

  All user interaction with the simulation and its results is managed by \ref
  qmc::MCStep "MCStep". This class allows the _spawning_ of simulation objects,
  and takes a \ref qmc::Lattice "Lattice" object instantiated by the user to
  perform necessary set-up steps. It manages:
  - Random number generators (RNGs)
  - Simulation data, stored dynamically at the adress qmc::MCStep::sse_data.
  - A \ref qmc::Lattice "Lattice" and set of \ref qmc::MCStep::observables_
    "observables" provided by the user.

  This class is meant to be used as an interface between the simulation and the
  various components it requires. It is not meant to model the physical system,
  the SSE storage or the observables in any way.
 */

